Spec: Mobile gateway owner interface

Purpose:
  Let the user enroll a device, inspect actual application identity and approve narrowly scoped access.

Owns:
  ./OwnerActivity.java

References:
  ./OwnerActions.sdd
  ./AndroidIdentity.sdd

Must:
  Present overview, devices, applications and settings as four stable destinations; keep daily start/stop on overview and enrollment/recovery in settings.
  Show actual gateway state without claiming P2P or service readiness from process presence; update state in place while resumed, preserving scroll and navigation.
  Use readable cards, bounded detail dialogs, loading/empty states and accessible touch targets that adapt to narrow, large-font and unfolded layouts.
  Keep full verified caller provenance and exact application/service facts reviewable before approval; condensed cards must not remove security confirmation or uncertain-operation recovery.
  Read identity/configuration status on the bounded worker without generating keys, resetting state or treating invalid storage as missing setup.
  Require explicit confirmation of root fingerprint, peer key and reviewed application/service facts before changes.
  Ignore administrative Intent extras and use user-selected public documents only.
  Keep application-provided labels separate from actual package/signing provenance and escape untrusted review text.
  Use bounded pages and background work, expose recovery for uncertain decisions and never auto-approve requests.
  Separate foreground start/stop from UI lifetime and require restart for certificate replacement.

  Confirm the server certificate fingerprint and explicit endpoints from a selected public document while stopped; show server mode and startup failure without exposing secrets.
